# La Settimana Possibile — the project itself has no build output.
# Everything below is local junk, not artefacts.

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# Tooling scratch (headless-browser runs, local servers)
.playwright-mcp/
node_modules/

# Locally generated printouts. Your own filled-in week is yours to keep off
# git; the one example PDF the project ships (empty, regenerated from
# index.html per AGENTS.md §6a) is tracked on purpose.
*.pdf
!examples/*.pdf

# A separate, undocumented sub-project (Python/Jinja2/Playwright canvas
# generator) that landed in this working directory from elsewhere. It isn't
# described anywhere in AGENTS.md/README.md, it also contains real filled-in
# personal data under data/weeks/ and examples/demo-weeks/2026-w35.json
# (mislabeled as a demo), and it pulls in exactly the build-step/dependency
# tooling AGENTS.md §1a says this repo doesn't have. Stays local until it's
# deliberately reviewed, cleaned of real data, and documented as an actual
# product of this repo — see the project owner's decision on 2026-08-31.
examples/settimana-possibile/

# Private planning data — a filled-in week is someone's real life, never a
# template. Same rule as the *.pdf exception above, applied to app/'s own
# local sample/export data.
app/data/
